			<div class="content" id="post-content-1529337">
									

<p>Personally, I prefer the &quot;slow-time&quot; version, as a horror from the perspective of the microcosm. Imagine the first few ships out: from the perspective of ground control, the ships just slow to a stop a certain distance above the map. The sense of despair as they think that they're trapped and doomed with nothing that can save them&#8230; until they realize that the ships are just operating incredibly slowly. And the reactions from the first crew: they turn around when they stop receiving transmissions from ground control, only to find that months have passed in the few minutes (from their perspective) that they were gone.</p>
<p>It's like the time dilation effect of near-luminal travel, only on an observable scale.</p>

